      "message": "While this prevents strange collisions, it does not actually put the child spans in order. It is possible that the user lists the children in one order and then draws them in the opposite order. Possible other approaches:\n\n1. Scan from last child to first child and ensure each span starts at the minimum seen so far. Then emit kids \"in order\".\n\n2. The simple approach of emit any kid that \"comes before\" the next child.",
